			"Message": "feat(Sky): Relay treeView.reveal to workbench view panel\n\nCocoon extensions calling `vscode.treeView.reveal(element)` dispatch a\n`sky://tree-view/reveal` URI that must open and focus the corresponding tree\nview panel in the workbench. Add a relay handler in InstallSimpleRelays that\nfires a `cel:tree-view:reveal` DOM event and invokes `Views.openView(viewId)`\non the workbench service layer.\n\nThe handler is guarded by a null check on viewId and a try/catch so the\nrelay pipeline is never interrupted when the workbench is not yet initialised.\nStale optional chaining on `openView` cleaned up (the outer try/catch already\ncovers rejection).",
			"SHA": "651bca38044971374a08dd5fab01e2cea093595a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T08:23:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Relay OSC 633 shell integration sequences from terminal data\n\nParse VS Code shell integration escape sequences (OSC 633) from terminal\noutput in the Sky bridge layer and forward them to Mountain via\nMountainIPCInvoke so Cocoon extensions can read\n`terminal.shellIntegration.cwd` and detect shell integration activation.\n\nOSC 633 ; A (prompt start) triggers `localPty:setShellIntegrationActive`\nonce per terminal; OSC 633 ; P ; cwd=<path> triggers `localPty:setCwd` on\neach CWD update. Parsing is guarded by a Set to avoid redundant activation\nnotifications and wraps all Tauri IPC in try/catch so terminal data\nrendering is never interrupted.\n\nExtends `InstallProgressTerminalWorkspace` in the Sky/Bridge layer.",
			"SHA": "42861a8462195fc313ca33f8e651cac53423a0ac"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T07:30:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Implement active terminal tracking and optimize extension manifest baking\n\nAdd logic to synchronize `vscode.window.activeTerminal` with the UI's active terminal instance by invoking the `localPty:setActive` Tauri command when the active terminal changes. This ensures accurate state tracking between the Cocoon extension host and the Sky workspace UI.\n\nEnable the `BakeExtensionManifest` plugin in all environments to maintain a warm extension cache in Mountain, reducing repeated dev build times to under 10ms once cached.",
			"SHA": "706316c94d57e5674d41361a384b346f4574d19f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T03:28:05Z",
